pe":"text","text":"The heavy–light decomposition of a rooted tree or arborescence: each vertex’s heavy child is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its child with the largest subtree (the first in "},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order on a tie), and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heavy edges form paths. Vertices get positions in a preorder that takes the heavy child first,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so each heavy path and each subtree is an interval of positions, and any path between two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices is at most 2⌊log₂ n⌋ + 1 intervals ("},{"code":"segments(from:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), for path and subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries over a structure indexed by position."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/heavylightdecomposition","kind":"symbol","title":"HeavyLightDecomposition"},"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms/HeavyLightDecomposition/segments(from:to:includingCommonAncestor:)":{"title":"segments(from:to:includingCommonAncestor:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"segments","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"includingCommonAncestor","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"HeavyLightDecomposition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14TreeAlgorit